==Battleground==
*3 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Gobble]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*4 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 8~10 seconds<sup>240f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**8 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**5 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**4 [[Gobble]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage combines the nasty nature of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies with extra Gobbles to take away portions of your units' health with his [[Toxic]] ability.

Stacking [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] or [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] is not very consistent here due to the starting Metal Doges, although you can still bring them. The best option is to use [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]] to brute-force the Metal enemies. A [[Talents|Talented]] [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] can potentially help against the Gobbles, but her high cost remains an issue. A [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] talented with Critical Hit is much better than Cyborg here, as her survive, better cost efficiency, strength against Gobble and potential to clear out every metal is much better, even if she doesn't have toxic immune.

[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] can be of great use here, dismantling Gobbles almost immediately when stacked and making the fight much easier.

==Trivia==
*Going along with the theme of meat and cooking in [[Rose-Colored Road]], the term used for "cloak" in Cloak of Hiding's Japanese name is ''mino'', which can refer to either a traditional Japanese raincoat made of straw or a cow's rumen.

